usage: - [-h] [--transport {stdio,streamable-http}] [--docker]
         [--docs-jsonl DOCS_JSONL] [--corpus-annoy PATH]
         [--corpus-embedding-model CORPUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL]
         [--hash-dimension HASH_DIMENSION] [--annoy-metric ANNOY_METRIC]
         [--annoy-n-trees ANNOY_N_TREES] [--host HOST] [--port PORT]
         [--path PATH] [--health-path HEALTH_PATH] [--no-health-endpoint]
         [--max-concurrency MAX_CONCURRENCY]
         [--max-request-body MAX_REQUEST_BODY] [--stateful-http]
         [--allow-unauthenticated-remote] [--probe]
         [--probe-timeout PROBE_TIMEOUT] [--print-effective-config]
         [--list-capabilities] [--self-test]
         [--self-test-query SELF_TEST_QUERY] [--self-test-require-match]
         [--self-test-expected-doc-id SELF_TEST_EXPECTED_DOC_ID]
         [--log-level {DEBUG,INFO,WARNING,ERROR,CRITICAL}]

Run or probe the scikitplot documentation MCP server

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --transport {stdio,streamable-http}
                        MCP transport; defaults to streamable-http with
                        --docker, otherwise stdio (default: None)
  --docker              Use container defaults: streamable-http, host 0.0.0.0,
                        and an enabled health route. This explicitly permits
                        the container-network bind but does not add
                        authentication. (default: False)
  --docs-jsonl DOCS_JSONL
                        Optional bounded JSONL corpus; built-in demo is the
                        default (default: None)
  --corpus-annoy PATH   Build a local scikitplot.corpus retriever from PATH
                        and force the Annoy vector backend. Uses the
                        deterministic HashEmbedder unless --corpus-embedding-
                        model is supplied. (default: None)
  --corpus-embedding-model CORPUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL
                        Optional model-backed embedding name for --corpus-
                        annoy. Omit for the deterministic offline
                        HashEmbedder. (default: None)
  --hash-dimension HASH_DIMENSION
                        HashEmbedder dimension used by --corpus-annoy when no
                        model is selected (default: None)
  --annoy-metric ANNOY_METRIC
                        Annoy metric used by --corpus-annoy (default: None)
  --annoy-n-trees ANNOY_N_TREES
                        Annoy tree count used by --corpus-annoy (default:
                        None)
  --host HOST           HTTP bind host (default: None)
  --port PORT           HTTP bind port (default: None)
  --path PATH           Streamable HTTP endpoint path (default: None)
  --health-path HEALTH_PATH
                        Unauthenticated HTTP health route; ignored by stdio
                        (default: None)
  --no-health-endpoint  Disable the HTTP health route (default: False)
  --max-concurrency MAX_CONCURRENCY
  --max-request-body MAX_REQUEST_BODY
  --stateful-http       Keep HTTP sessions; stateless is default (default:
                        False)
  --allow-unauthenticated-remote
                        Explicitly permit a non-local bind without
                        authentication (default: False)
  --probe               GET the configured health endpoint and exit instead of
                        starting a server (default: False)
  --probe-timeout PROBE_TIMEOUT
                        Health-probe timeout in seconds (default: None)
  --print-effective-config
                        Print validated effective configuration as JSON and
                        exit (default: False)
  --list-capabilities   Print the read-only tool/resource inventory as JSON
                        and exit (does not import the MCP SDK or start a
                        server) (default: False)
  --self-test           Load the configured backend, run one deterministic
                        read-only search, validate the output contract, print
                        JSON, and exit (default: False)
  --self-test-query SELF_TEST_QUERY
                        Query used by --self-test (default: None)
  --self-test-require-match
                        Fail --self-test when the query returns zero passages
                        (default: False)
  --self-test-expected-doc-id SELF_TEST_EXPECTED_DOC_ID
                        Fail --self-test unless this exact citation doc_id is
                        returned (default: None)
  --log-level {DEBUG,INFO,WARNING,ERROR,CRITICAL}
delegate_exit=0
